/-!
# The genuine local relative Fourier homotopy

For the original varying period family, the actual closedness equations
of a smooth triple imply an actual local normal form. The selected
holomorphic inverse Fourier series removes all nonzero modes, and the
genuine Cauchy--Green primitive removes the remaining base mean. The only
residual components are the two original vertical Haar means, which are
proved holomorphic in the original base.

All sums, derivatives, and means are the original analytic objects. This
package does not yet identify every native closed differential-form
section with such a triple, or assert a higher-direct-image frame.
-/
